SUMMARY:Directors' Cut
DESCRIPTION:Four directors\, twenty years\, and one building that didn’t always exist. \nLong before BIC had a building to call its own\, it was but an idea. This conversation turns the lens on the institution itself\, bringing together four directors to reflect on the different Bangalore International Centres they each inherited\, built\, and passed on. Structured as an AMA\, the session draws questions from RSVPs\, from BIC’s own staff\, and from the audience in the room. \nFrom an institution without walls\, to the construction and induction of its home\, to the shaping of the team that runs it today\, and now\, into its next chapter — this open\, unscripted conversation looks at what it takes to build and sustain an institution like this one\, and what each director would like to see it become. \nThis talk is part of a series marking twenty years of BIC. It is a chance to trace what has changed\, what has endured\, and how ideas evolve over time. BIC is proud to have been host to conversations that connect culture\, ideas\, and public life across two decades. \nLink to Architecting India’s Legacy Report\, a casestudy of BIC and IIC. \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nTwenty Years On: Revisiting Voices from BIC’s Founding Years\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSceyBpBfTXQLBuLKeXdTluyi21xu8hZaRZ8jO_TNvp44nnNNA/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: P. R. Dasgupta\, V. Ravichandar\, Vikram Bhat\, Anupama Sekhar\n*Event Categories*: Bangalore\, Governance\, History\, Management
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/directors-cut/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Bangalore,Governance,History,Management
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail_DC.jpg
END:VEVENT
