SUMMARY:The Ocean Between Us
DESCRIPTION:\n \nThe Ocean Between Us is a cross-cultural\, immersive movement theatre project grounded in contemporary dance and writing. The work treats the body as a vessel for communication\, connection\, and care: a space to wrestle with difficult questions. Who are we beyond the labels\, and how do we bridge the “ocean” of race\, gender\, economics\, and identity that divides us? \nThe collaboration began as a self-designed Instagram residency\, the artists responding to questions as intimate as they were unanswerable: how can I listen so I can hear you? Where does it hurt? What are you afraid of? Later deepened across each other’s countries and shared through workshops in India and Australia\, their practice shaped a methodology that brings tenderness into moments of conflict and clashing perspectives. Raw\, fragmented\, and resistant to linear logic\, the work invites audiences into the mess of these questions\, and into the possibility of rest. \nIn collaboration with: \n \n\nSupported by: \n \nVenue: Gallery\n\n\nA Movement Theatre Piece\nFor Ages 16+\nRSVPs closed. Thank you for your interest.\n*Performers*: Diya Naidu\, Nadia Milford\n*Event Categories*: Dance\, Performing Arts\, Theatre
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-ocean-between-us/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Dance,Performing Arts,Theatre
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail_TOBU.jpg
END:VEVENT
